                         ‍‍Orders for substitutions of prescribed medications will only be processed if the prescribing physician has expressly authorized the dispensing of an equivalent generic drug in place of the prescribed brand-name drug, if the prescription specifies only the generic salt names, or if the physician has indicated on the prescription that substitution is permitted. If neither condition is met, the Pharmacy will not process a substitution. Users acknowledge that in such instances the responsibility for substitution authorizations rests solely with the prescribing physician.

